            "review_title": "Review at Seafood Nam Ranh",
            "review_text": "スロバンカー\nTokyo, Japan84 contributions\n0\nA restaurant in a private home like this? A great value seafood restaurant that you'll want to visit at least once\nDec 2023 • Solo\nIf you want to eat cheap and delicious seafood in Da Nang, this is the perfect place for you.\n\nIt's in a residential area that's hard to find. It's hard to get in by car, so I recommend driving close by or taking a grab bike. I went there by grab bike.\n\nThe restaurant was quite busy even though it was just before closing time. There were backpackers from all over the world and Westerners.\n\nThere were surprisingly few Vietnamese people.\n\nThe menu is also in Japanese lol\n\nThe lobster was 1,000,000 VND, or about 6,000 yen, so I ordered limefish, a fish I'd never tried before\n\nsnails with garlic butter!\n\nThe limefish looked spiky, but it was light and had a light white flesh. The snails were hard to taste because the garlic butter was too strong, but they were delicious!\nEven though I drank a lot of beer, the bill didn't go up that much, so it's definitely a good place ^_^\nYou can enjoy seafood with an emphasis on atmosphere along the beach in Da Nang, or you can eat seafood in a remote place with an emphasis on value for money! It's up to your preference! The staff were also very friendly!\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten December 28, 2023",
